verdicts.impact:
The spec defines the error (SwInvalidConfig via hmac_err) but not what 'blocked' does to the rest of the state. One engineer might check only the error and that hmac_done stays low, as the existing test does. Another might also check any of the following, and could reasonably expect different values:
- the engine stays idle;
- later MSG_FIFO writes are dropped, or accepted and counted in MSG_LENGTH;
- a following CMD.hash_process is ignored;
- the previous DIGEST contents are kept or cleared;
- whether a later valid start needs a fresh hash_start.
